<font color=white>When duty calls... Part II</font></td>
<td align=right bgcolor=#333333>
<nowrap><font color=white>Posted by <A HREF="/index.pl?node_id=1782&lastnode_id=1939">Slackjaw</a> on 2001-06-23 22:52:14</font></nowrap></td></tr>
<tr><td colspan=2>I greet you my brothers and sisters of the Horde...<br>
<br>
I hope it did not take to long for this message to get to you. In my last letter i told you that i had a vision of Innoruuk and a quest i should have to forfill. Many things have happened after that.....<br>
<br>
After spending my last night in the Maiden's Fancy in Neriak's third gate, I got up early next morning to head for Neriak Commons to prepare myself for my forthcoming quest.. After selecting the best gear i've got and getting enough food and water supplies to make the long trip, I made my way to Neriak Foreign Quarter. This is where i met my first two companions. Braneal en Tdar, a dark elf warrior and shadowknight. They to had a vision of Lord Innorruuk, in which he said to head for Iceclad to forfill an important task. So together we travelled trough Nektulos Forest, East Commonlands to end up in the Desert of North Ro where or boat should be waiting.<br>
<br>
Upon arrivel at the docks we met the rest of our group.<br>
<br>
Cikis an Iksar Necromancer, Rrak an Iksar Warrior, Rakolog and Ogre warrior, Obok another Ogre warrior, Kakal an Troll Shadowknight and last but not least Ramn an other Troll Shadowknight. He was also with me the night we killed the dwarven king..<br>
<br>
All of us had seen the same vision of Lord Innoruuk..<br>
<br>
When the ship arrived, we all boarded the ship, and were finally heading for Iceclad. I've sailed many ships before, but never seen anything like this. I am still amazed we all survived the trip to Iceclad on this..... ehm thing.<br>
<br>
At this moment we have arrived on Velious and are waiting for any sign of or Lord.<br>
<br>
This is were this letter end's<br>
<br>
<br>
I will contact you as soon as possible again my friends.<br>
<br>
Greetings..<br>
Slackjaw Lengkaef</td></tr><tr><td colspan=2>&nbsp;</td></tr>


